    "details": "Mongoose is an embedded web server and network library. Prior to 7.22, an attacker who can control an SSI-enabled file can place directory traversal sequences in an #include file or #include virtual directive. The `mg_ssi()` function in `src/ssi.c` concatenates the directive argument into a filesystem path without calling `mg_path_is_sane()`, allowing an `MG_ENABLE_SSI` deployment with `ssi_pattern` configured to disclose files readable by the Mongoose process. This issue is fixed in version 7.22.",
